<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	P1 scope: no CloudKit, no push, no CarPlay. iOS apps have no App
	Sandbox concept (`com.apple.security.*` sandbox keys are macOS-only —
	iOS network access needs no entitlement at all), so there was nothing
	to declare at P1; this file is the wiring point for whatever P2+
	actually needs (push for gatekeeper approvals, etc.).

	P6 "Widgets" task (plan §Platform parity): added the App Group
	capability — see EnchiridionMac.entitlements' comment for the full
	rationale (same identifier, same shared `LocalGraphStore` file, shared
	with the new `Enchiridion2iOSWidget` extension target). The
	`com.apple.security.application-groups` key works identically on iOS
	despite iOS having no sandbox-key concept otherwise — App Groups is its
	own capability, not part of `com.apple.security.app-sandbox`.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.dev.rawkode.enchiridion2</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
